# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/

# Env / secrets — never commit (HANDOFF.md 3: secrets live in AWS Secrets Manager)
.env
.env.*

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# OS
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini


# Owner rule: markdown files are not committed — EXCEPT docs/, which holds
# the load-bearing project artifacts (design docs, calibration file,
# deploy runbook, design-system guidelines). Root-level and apps-level
# *.md stay ignored. Owner ruling 2026-09-19: the per-file sanctioned-
# exception gate has done its job; docs/ is a standing allowlist now.
*.md
!docs/**

# Node (apps/web)
node_modules/
dist/

# MEMORY_BANK.md is a sanctioned exception to the *.md ignore (owner ruling):
# it is the live codebase-intelligence file at project root, force-added once and
# thereafter tracked by this negation so future commits need no --force.
!MEMORY_BANK.md

.vite/
.tanstack/

# Build / dev artifacts
*.log
*.png

!apps/web/.env.example

# Owner-supplied benchmark corpus (copyrighted judgments) — never commit
/fixtures/

# Cline workspace files — local only
.clinerules
.continue/
